<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Mandela returns six weeks after finishing 37 fractions of radiotherapy, which he completed without a break. In the fourth week he developed urinary frequency, a weaker stream, and getting up twice a night, and radiation oncology started tamsulosin 0.4 mg in the evening; these symptoms are now improving, and he has had no burning, blood in the urine, or retention, and no dizziness on standing. In the last weeks of treatment his bowels became looser, two or three times a day with some urgency, and they are now settling to once or twice a day, with no bleeding. Asked about his bowels before treatment, he says they were regular, about once a day, as recorded at his wellness visit. His second leuprolide depot ran out about three weeks ago; hot flashes are fewer, and the tiredness he had during radiotherapy is lifting. His mood is good. He has resumed his morning walks. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Radiotherapy</td><td>74 Gy in 37 fractions, completed six weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Urinary</td><td>Frequency and nocturia twice, improving on tamsulosin; no blood or burning</td></tr><tr><td>Bowel</td><td>Looser stools and mild urgency, settling; no bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Androgen deprivation</td><td>Completed; last depot ran out three weeks ago; hot flashes fading</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

